    "id": "0011-transfer-of-learning",
    "batchId": "batch-001",
    "categoryCode": "00",
    "fieldCode": "0011",
    "fieldTitle": "Basic programmes and qualifications",
    "fieldTitleZh": "基础课程与资格",
    "title": "The Bend That Wasn't on the Table",
    "titleZh": "桌面上没有的弯",
    "summary": "The academy's best model-bridge builder carries his prize plan to a real river that refuses to follow the classroom current.",
    "summaryZh": "最会搭模型桥的学徒把获奖图纸带到真河边，河水却没有照着教室里的路线流。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "Every year, Stonebridge Academy asked its students to build bridges on wooden tables. Blue cloth marked the river, stones marked the banks, and a teacher poured a narrow current from a jug. Yizhen had won the exercise three years in a row. When a flood took the old bridge east of town, the mayor put him in charge of a temporary replacement.",
      "Yizhen brought his prize drawing to the river. The plan placed a pier in midstream, so that was where he ordered the workers to drive it. An old ferryman warned him that the river made a sharp turn upstream and pushed timber toward the eastern bank in high water. Yizhen looked at the straight lines on his drawing and said the academy had tested the design many times.",
      "The first pier leaned during the night. There was only enough money to drive it once more, and Yizhen wanted to dig deeper in the same place. The ferryman did not argue. He threw a dead branch into the river. It drifted toward the centre, then swung sideways at the bend and struck the leaning pier.",
      "Yizhen rolled up his drawing and walked upstream. He touched old flood marks on trees along the eastern bank and found broken reeds packed into the rocks. The next morning, he moved the pier, angled the bridge into the current, and added another cable on the eastern side.",
      "When the new bridge opened, Yizhen did not wait at the entrance for praise. He went underneath, put one hand on the added cable, and listened as the first grain cart crossed the boards above him."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "石桥学院每年都让学生在木桌上搭桥。桌面铺着蓝布，石块代表河岸，老师还会从水壶里倒出一股细流。易真连续三年得了第一。镇东的旧桥被洪水冲坏后，镇长便把临时桥交给了他。",
      "易真带着获奖图纸来到河边。图上桥墩应立在河心，他便叫工人照做。老艄公提醒他，这条河在上游转了一个急弯，涨水时会把木头推向东岸。易真看着笔直的图线，只说学院已经试过很多次。",
      "第一根桥墩当晚便歪了。工钱只够再打一次，易真仍想把同一位置挖得更深。老艄公没有争辩，只把一截枯枝丢进水里。枯枝先向河心漂，到了弯口突然横过来，撞上那根桥墩。",
      "易真收起图纸，沿河走到上游。他摸到东岸树干上的旧水痕，又看见石缝里塞满折断的芦苇。第二天，他把桥墩移开，让桥身斜着迎向水流，并在东岸多加一道拉索。",
      "新桥开放那天，易真没有站在桥头等人夸奖。他走到桥下，扶着那道拉索，听第一辆粮车从木板上慢慢驶过。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Transfer of learning",
    "conceptNameZh": "学习迁移",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "Transfer of learning occurs when knowledge or skill gained in one setting improves performance in another. It is not the simple copying of familiar steps. Learners must recognise the principle that still applies beneath a different surface and adjust their method to new conditions. Comparing varied cases, explaining why a method works, and practising when to use it all support transfer."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "学习迁移是把一种情境中获得的知识或技能有效用于另一种情境。它不是照搬熟悉步骤，而是识别不同表面下仍然成立的原理，并根据新条件调整做法。比较多种案例、解释方法为何有效，以及练习判断何时使用，都会帮助迁移发生。"
    ],
