    "id": "0221-sacred-and-profane",
    "batchId": "batch-003",
    "categoryCode": "02",
    "fieldCode": "0221",
    "fieldTitle": "Religion and theology",
    "fieldTitleZh": "宗教与神学",
    "title": "One Well on Two Kinds of Day",
    "titleZh": "一口井的两种日子",
    "summary": "An ordinary market well cannot be used for tea on one day each year, and a travelling merchant arrives with his bucket.",
    "summaryZh": "集市上的普通水井每年有一天不能用来卖茶，一名外乡人偏偏在那天提来了水桶。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "A well stood at the centre of White Stone. On ordinary days, tea sellers drew from it, children washed their hands on the rim, and drivers filled troughs for their animals. Only on the anniversary of an old fire did the town remove the bucket and place twelve empty cups beside the well for those who had never returned.",
      "A travelling tea merchant named Luping encountered the anniversary for the first time. Not knowing the custom, he lowered his bucket as usual. Several townspeople stopped him. Looking into the water, Luping said that the water used for tea yesterday had not changed today. The keeper did not claim that it had. He simply set the twelve cups upright again.",
      "That summer brought drought, and the town's other well dried up first. On the anniversary morning, people arrived in the square with empty jars. Some insisted that the memorial well remain untouched all day; others said the living needed water. The argument continued as the sun rose, with the twelve cups still on the rim.",
      "At last, the families of the dead each drew one cup and poured it beneath the old tree. Then they returned the bucket to the rope and allowed each household to take a turn. The tea stalls remained closed, but the well did not.",
      "Luping waited until last. After filling his jar, he did not set up his stove. He placed his own cup beside the other twelve."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "白石镇中央有一口井。平日里，茶摊从那里取水，孩子在井沿洗手，赶车人也会给牲口添满水槽。只有旧火灾纪念日，镇民会撤下木桶，在井边摆十二只空杯，记住当年没有回来的人。",
      "外乡茶商陆平第一次赶上纪念日。他不知道规矩，照常放下水桶。几名镇民立刻拦住他。陆平看着井水说，昨天能煮茶的水，今天并没有变。守井人也没有说水变了，只把那十二只空杯重新摆正。",
      "那年夏天大旱，镇里另一口井先干了。纪念日清晨，许多人带着空罐来到广场。有人坚持整日不能动井，有人说活着的人也需要水。争论持续到太阳升高，十二只杯子仍放在井沿。",
      "最后，遇难者家属先各舀一杯水，倒在老树根下。随后，他们把木桶挂回井绳，让每户按次序取水。茶摊那天没有开，井却没有封住。",
      "陆平排到最后。他提满水罐后，没有支起茶炉，只把自己带来的杯子放在那十二只杯子旁边。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Sacred and profane",
    "conceptNameZh": "神圣与世俗",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "The distinction between sacred and profane separates things treated through special meaning, obligation, prohibition, or ritual from the realm of ordinary activity. The difference need not arise from a material change; it is created, maintained, and contested through shared practice. Sacred does not automatically mean good, nor profane evil, and boundaries vary with tradition and circumstance."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "神圣与世俗之分把受到特殊意义、义务、禁令或仪式对待的事物，与日常活动领域区分开来。差别不一定来自物质变化，而由共同实践建立、维持并争论。神圣不自动等于善，世俗也不等于恶；边界会随传统与处境而变化。"
    ],
    "mode": "concept-fable",
    "status": "approved",
    "qualityGate": {
      "reviewRounds": 3,
      "rewriteRounds": 2,
      "openCritical": 0,
      "openMajor": 0
    },
