    "explanation": "Source criticism asks who created a record, when, for whom, for what purpose, and how it was preserved or derived, in order to judge what claims it can support. A partial or mistaken source can still be useful. Historical work corroborates independent traces, explains disagreement, and states uncertainty rather than automatically trusting one type of record.",
    "explanationZh": "史料批判考察材料由谁、何时、为谁、出于何种目的制作，又如何保存和相互依赖，以判断它能支持什么主张。带立场或含错误的材料仍可能有价值。历史研究通过互证、解释分歧和标明不确定性，而非自动相信某一种来源。"
