    "fieldTitleZh": "社会学与文化研究",
    "title": "The Empty Bench on a Full Ferry",
    "titleZh": "满船上的空长椅",
    "summary": "The ferry is too crowded to turn around, yet the long bench at the bow remains empty.",
    "summaryZh": "渡船已经挤得无人能转身，船头那张长椅却仍然空着。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "A long bench stood at the bow of the Green Bay ferry. No sign said who could sit there, yet passengers knew it was reserved for guild elders. Even when no elder travelled, ordinary people remained standing. Anyone who moved too close received coughs, stares, or a warning not to ignore custom.",
      "One stormy day, other crossings closed and the cabin filled. A stonemason named Aman, whose leg was bandaged, sat on the bench. The ticket collector did not stop him, but passengers immediately began talking. Some complained that young people had become selfish, while others refused to pass his baggage along.",
      "At the next stop, a guild elder boarded. Aman prepared to rise, but the elder saw his injury and sat on a wooden box. Several passengers still urged Aman to move, as though the elder's own choice could not cancel the unwritten rule.",
      "The elder asked who had established the bench. No one could answer. They only remembered that a passenger had once been condemned by the whole ferry for refusing to move. The elder sat beside Aman and placed his luggage between them. No one coughed during the remaining crossing.",
      "There was still no new sign the next day. A man carrying a child sat first, and a nearby passenger moved his bag closer to his feet."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "青湾渡船的船头有一张长椅。没有告示规定谁能坐，乘客却都知道那是留给行会长老的。即使长老不在，普通人也宁愿站着。有人靠得太近，旁边乘客便会咳嗽、盯视，或提醒他“别不懂规矩”。",
      "一天风雨封了其他渡口，船舱挤得满满当当。腿上缠着绷带的石匠阿满坐上长椅。售票员没有阻止，周围乘客却立刻议论。有人说年轻人越来越自私，还有人故意不替他传递行李。",
      "下一站，行会长老上船。阿满正要起身，长老看见他的伤，坐到了木箱上。几名乘客仍催阿满让座，仿佛长老本人的选择也不能取消这条没有写下的规矩。",
      "长老问是谁定下这张椅子。没人答得出，只记得曾有人因不让座被全船责骂。长老随后坐到阿满身边，把自己的行李放在两人中间。余下航程里，再没有人咳嗽。",
      "第二天，长椅上仍没有新告示。一个抱着孩子的男人先坐了下来，旁边的人看了一眼，替他把行李推到脚边。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Norm enforcement",
    "conceptNameZh": "规范执行",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "Norm enforcement maintains shared expectations through approval, reminders, shame, exclusion, punishment, or sanctions against those who fail to intervene, often without written law. Enforcement may be distributed among peers or organised formally. A persistent norm is not necessarily fair; power, visibility, and unequal ability to sanction shape who is constrained."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "规范执行通过赞许、提醒、羞辱、排斥、惩罚或制裁不干预者来维持共同期待，往往无需成文法律。执行可以分散在同伴之间，也可能由正式机构承担。规范持续存在不代表它公平；权力、可见性和制裁能力会决定谁更容易被约束。"
    ],
