    "id": "0521-tragedy-of-the-commons",
    "batchId": "batch-007",
    "categoryCode": "05",
    "fieldCode": "0521",
    "fieldTitle": "Environmental sciences",
    "fieldTitleZh": "环境科学",
    "title": "One More Sheep",
    "titleZh": "再多一只羊",
    "summary": "Each household adds only one sheep to the common pasture, and no one can see how their own animal makes the grass disappear.",
    "summaryZh": "每户只往公共牧场多放一只羊，谁都看不出自己怎样让草消失。",
    "storyParagraphs": [
      "River Village shared one pasture. In good years, each household kept ten sheep there. When lamb prices rose, the first family added one more. Its extra income would be private, while the small loss of grass would be spread across every flock.",
      "Other households saw and added one as well. No family increased by much, but dozens of sheep appeared. By summer, roots could not recover and rain carried away bare soil. Every household said its final sheep could not have damaged the whole pasture.",
      "The next year, the village neither abolished common ownership nor relied on appeals to restraint. Users and seasons were defined, and herders jointly set numbers. They rotated grass-height checks. Excess first received a warning and then a reduced share the next season, with disputes reviewed publicly.",
      "The rules still required judgement. A family losing animals to disease requested a temporary adjustment and received one based on current grass. Sheep placed there by outsiders were removed. The pasture remained shared, but private gain could no longer disperse unlimited damage.",
      "Before spring grazing, each household led out its flock and wrote the number on the entrance board. After the final sheep passed, the keeper lowered the bar."
    ],
    "storyParagraphsZh": [
      "河村的牧场归全村使用。草多的年份，每户都能养十只羊。羊羔价格上涨后，第一户多放了一只，觉得新增收入归自己，而少掉的一点草由全村羊群共同承担。",
      "其他人看见后也各加一只。没有哪一家单独增加很多，牧场上的羊却迅速多出几十只。入夏后，草根来不及恢复，裸土被雨冲走。每户都说自己的最后一只羊不可能造成整片牧场变坏。",
      "第二年，村里没有简单禁止共有牧场，也没有只劝大家自觉。他们先划清使用者和季节边界，让牧户共同决定数量；轮流检查草高，超量者先警告、再逐步罚减下一季份额，争议可当场复核。",
      "规则并非毫无冲突。遭遇病羊的一户申请临时补充，牧户根据实际草况调整；外村偷放的羊则被赶出。牧场仍由大家共有，却不再允许收益私拿、退化成本无限分散。",
      "春天放牧前，每户牵出羊群，在入口木牌上写下数目。最后一只羊经过以后，守牧人落下了门栓。"
    ],
    "conceptName": "Tragedy of the commons",
    "conceptNameZh": "公地悲剧",
    "explanationParagraphs": [
      "The tragedy of the commons is a dilemma in which users receive much of the gain from additional use of a rival shared resource while spreading degradation costs across the group, encouraging overuse. Depletion is not inevitable under common ownership; clear boundaries, user participation, monitoring, graduated sanctions, and dispute resolution can support durable governance."
    ],
    "explanationParagraphsZh": [
      "公地悲剧是共享且具有竞争性的资源中，个体获得新增使用的大部分收益，却把退化成本分散给群体，导致过度使用的困境。耗竭并非共有产权的必然结果；清晰边界、使用者参与、监督、渐进制裁和争议解决可支持持久治理。"
    ],
    "mode": "concept-fable",
    "status": "approved",
    "qualityGate": {
      "reviewRounds": 3,
      "rewriteRounds": 2,
      "openCritical": 0,
      "openMajor": 0
    },
    "collection": "field-core-fables",
