    "explanation": "Base-rate reasoning in diagnosis combines a test result with the tested population's probability of disease before testing. Even with high sensitivity and specificity, a small false-positive rate applied to many healthy people can make false positives a large share of positive results when disease is rare. Bayesian updating, likelihood ratios, and confirmation pathways translate test performance into an individual's post-test probability.",
