    "explanation": "Dignity of risk recognizes that informed and reasonable risk-taking is part of adult autonomy, identity, participation, and growth. Practice requires accessible information, decision support, individualized assessment, and proportionate measures to reduce avoidable harm while respecting legal limits and others' rights. It is neither blanket prohibition in the name of safety nor abandonment of care responsibility; deviations should prompt evidence-based review.",
    "explanationZh": "风险尊严承认，知情且合理的风险承担是成年人自主、身份、参与和成长的一部分。实践中应提供可及信息与决策支持，进行个体化评估，并用相称措施降低可避免伤害，同时尊重合法限制和他人权利。它既不是以安全名义全面禁止，也不是放弃照护责任；偏差发生后仍应按证据复核。"
