    "explanation": "Colour theory and oxidation connect starting pigment and level, added hue, reflected light, fibre condition, and chemical reaction. Oxidative colouring can alter natural melanin and form dye molecules within the fibre; old artificial colour, porosity, and prior damage change outcomes. A colour wheel supports neutralization decisions but cannot replace consultation, strand and skin-safety tests, product instructions, or the hair's tolerance limits.",
    "explanationZh": "色彩理论与氧化过程把起始色素、明度、加入色相、反射光、纤维状态和化学反应联系起来。氧化染色可改变天然黑色素并在纤维内部形成染料分子；旧人工色、孔隙和既往损伤会改变结果。色轮帮助理解中和，却不能替代咨询、发束与皮肤安全测试、产品说明和头发承受限制。"
