    "explanation": "Layered security coordinates people, processes, physical measures, and technology so one failure does not directly expose assets, people, or operations. Layers need clear functions, sufficiently independent failure modes, tested handoffs, and executable response and recovery; more layers do not automatically mean stronger protection. Design must also preserve proportionality, maintenance, accessibility, privacy, and life safety and avoid common dependencies that defeat several layers together.",
    "explanationZh": "分层防护协调人员、流程、物理和技术控制，让一次失效不会直接暴露资产、人员或运行。各层需有明确功能、足够独立的失效方式、经过测试的交接，以及可执行的响应与恢复；层数多不等于保护强。设计还要兼顾相称性、维护、可及性、隐私与生命安全，避免共同依赖同时击败多层。"
